# hooks/hooks.json is NOT ignored, and that is deliberate. Claude Code reads the
# hook wiring from that exact path, so a repository without it installs from a
# marketplace and then does nothing at all — no presence, no guards, no
# messages, and no error to explain it. The committed copy is the shell entry
# point, which is right everywhere bash exists. The installer overwrites it with
# the Python one on hosts without a shell, and that copy has an interpreter path
# baked in, so on those machines it shows up as a local modification.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Kept on this machine, never published. The repository is public and these
# files quote a private product codebase — branch names, PR numbers, entity
# ids, somebody else's bugs. They are the record of what actually happened when
# several sessions worked one repository for a day, which is worth having and
# is not ours to hand out. See notes/README.md.
notes/

# A third-party design skill, installed here so the dashboard can be worked on
# with it. Deliberately not committed. The README promises "Python 3.8+ and
# nothing else — no daemon, no service, no dependencies", and a hundred and
# fifty vendored files that need Node, sitting in the shipped tree, contradict
# that on sight for a tool only ever used while designing. It is somebody else's
# code as well, and republishing it under this repository's MIT licence is not a
# decision this file should make quietly.
#
# `npx impeccable install` puts it back. It lands in `.github/skills` when that
# directory exists and Claude Code reads `.agents/skills`, so it has to be moved.
# Anything under `.agents/context/` is OURS — written here, about this project —
# and is not ignored.
.agents/skills/
.agents/agents/
.impeccable/
